# Implementation Plan - Trend Badge Fix

The goal is to ensure the trend badges (total and scope-specific) are always accurate and never "disappear" or show stale data when switching between goals and base years.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Dashboard UI - dashboard.html

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.html)
- Add `id="trend-badge-total"` to the main trend badge.
- Add `id="trend-badge-scope1"` and `id="trend-badge-scope2"` to the scope breakdown badges.
- Remove hardcoded static trend values (e.g., "↓ 3.8%").

### [Component Name] Dashboard Logic - dashboard.js

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.js)
- Refactor [updateHeroMetrics](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.js#382-449) to:
    - Centralize trend calculation into a helper function (handling base year or goal fallbacks).
    - Update all three badges (total, scope 1, scope 2) using the same logic.
    - Ensure "—" is shown only when absolutely no data/goal/base-year is available.
    - Set colors consistently (success for reduction, danger for increase).

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- **Scenario 1**: Set a base year with data. Verify all three badges show the trend vs. that base year.
- **Scenario 2**: Set a base year with NO data, but have a goal. Verify badges fall back to showing progress vs. goal.
- **Scenario 3**: Have no base year and no goal. Verify badges show "—".
